<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-380-2026-11-29 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-380 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. T0 is the window open 2026-11-29T04:39:00Z (Sat 28 Nov 8:39 p.m. PT). SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf380 : four-hour window, page header 28 Nov 23:39 ET to 29 Nov 03:39 ET (04:39Z-08:39Z). Backup Sun 29 Nov 6:26 p.m. PT = 2026-11-30T02:26:00Z. 27th flight of the first stage. Landing on Of Course I Still Love You. LL2 id b0d27def-0a88-44c3-a947-1fd5b8503e2c status Go, NET 2026-11-29T04:39:00Z, window 04:39-08:39Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-26T11:45:38Z.
Published timeline (SpaceX ussf380): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:57, entry burn 6:04-6:27, landing burn 8:02, landing 8:25. SECO, orbit and deploy are not published. Payload is classified. No satellite count is used. SpaceX does not name the booster serial.
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, the same Iridium NEXT-7 altitude and downrange rows as USSF-266 / USSF-317 / USSF-627, laid on this flight&#x27;s azimuth. https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207
  MECO T+146 s and SES-1 T+156 s match this flight. Fairing on this page is T+177 s; the family loft samples fairing at T+176 s (1 s earlier). FILE ENDS AT T+508 s (telemetry end).
Azimuth 153.18 deg: great-circle bearing from the LL2 SLC-4E pad to the midpoint of the downrange edge of NAVAREA XII 836/26 Area A. Edge 32-05.00N 119-08.00W to 32-30.00N 119-18.00W. Midpoint 32.2917N 119.2167W. Bearing unrounded 153.184 deg, rounded to 153.18. Distance 290.6 km. https://www.sealagom.com/navarea/12/message/26135/836-26-north-pacific/
  Non-rotating inclination from 153.18 deg is 68.21 deg. Areas B and C of the same notice are further downrange (centroids about 154.32 deg and 155.11 deg) and were not used for the azimuth. No ZLA CARF polygon for 29 Nov was retrieved. The Area A polygon is the same shape USSF-317 recorded for NAVAREA XII 785/26 and did not use; this file uses it because it is the notice in force for USSF-380.
ASSUMPTION: SECO-1 at T+519 s and a 177.3 x 266.2 km parking orbit are borrowed from the Starlink Group 15 / USSF-317 config, not from USSF-380. LL2 says the drop zones match previous Starlink Group 15 launches. Inclination is not tuned. ILLUSTRATIVE.
Velocity = backward difference of ECEF position (Earth-relative). Pad (LL2): 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=153.18 deg from pad (spherical R=6371.0088 km).
T0 used: 2026-11-29T04:39:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
